    <summary>A spatial file manager for Windows.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[FileSpacer is a file manager for Windows built around the spatial paradigm: each folder has a single window that remembers its position, size and view settings. It is forked from ChromaFiler and distributed under the GPL v3 license.

### Features

- **One window per folder.** Its position, size, view mode and icon positions are remembered. Icons can be arranged freely or aligned to the standard positioning grid.
- **Window organization.** Opening another folder closes the source window by default. Hold Ctrl while opening a folder to keep the source window open. Windows without a saved position are placed to limit overlap.
- **Manage windows.** Move or resize windows using configurable mouse shortcuts. Save and reopen groups of folders, and lock window layouts.

![Three folder windows with different sizes, view modes and icon layouts.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LeBenco/FileSpacer/v@VERSION@/docs/en/images/spatial-windows.png)

FileSpacer supports Windows 10 or later (x64) and is available in ten languages, including English. It has no telemetry, usage tracking or advertising. Optional Everything integration provides indexed file search.

### Package information

This package downloads the official GitHub installer, verifies its SHA-256 and installs for all users. Existing native upgrade choices are preserved. It does not request a change of default file manager.]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/LeBenco/FileSpacer/releases/tag/v@VERSION@</releaseNotes>
    <tags>filespacer spatial file-manager windows explorer</tags>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
